<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JD Group half yr shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>JD Group half yr shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		99.0	  vs 86.1</p>
<p>    - attrib		  101.0	 vs 86.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 30.0	  vs 26.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   105.80	 vs    89.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   163.09	 vs   137.08</p>
<p>    Tax			  57.29	 vs    47.98</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    40.40	 vs    45.01</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,2901.11	 vs 1,248.96</p>
<p>Div payable April 16</p>
<p>on register March 14</p>
<p>Full name: JD Group Ltd (furniture, household and allied)</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said capitalisation shares will be awarded to shareholders.</p>
<p>They said difficult trading conditions would continue for the remainder of the financial year, although further improvements in operating margins and reductions in finance costs should translate into acceptable real earnings growth.</p>
<p>This growth would be accompanied by an enhancement in the quality of the debtor's book and a decline in the gearing ratio.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
